4. THIRD-PARTY DATA AND SERVICES

   The Work contains no map data. It can be pointed at third-party providers of
   imagery, terrain, street-level photography and geocoding. Those providers
   license their data separately and on their own terms, and most require an
   account, an API key, visible attribution and a cap on caching. Obtaining,
   reading and obeying those terms is entirely Your responsibility, and the
   Licensor grants You no right whatsoever to any third-party data. The Work
   ships with provider slots empty and defaults to locally generated terrain for
   exactly this reason.

   Third-party software components bundled with or required by the Work remain
   under their own licences; see THIRD-PARTY.md.

